## Nachtrag 2026-08-06

Die Fixtures `t/data/n-fixtures/l-calls.go` und `N-calls.go` brauchen
`//go:build ignore` als erste Zeile. Grund: `go.mod` liegt im Repo-Root
(Entscheidung in Ticket 4), damit gehört jede `.go`-Datei im Repo zum Modul
und würde von `go build ./...` übersetzt. Die Fixtures sind absichtlich
grenzwertig und dürfen das nicht.
Implemented. lib/Locale/Simple/Scraper/Parser.pm: new type go — concat_op='+'; literal_forms gets [", double_quote_string_contents, "] (reused as-is, go's normal double-quote escapes are no different from pl/js/py/tx) + a new go_backtick_string_contents wrapper (raw_string_contents('`') — static close delimiter, so unlike php's heredoc it fits the plain [open,content,close] triple with just a one-line wrapper since raw_string_contents takes its stop as an arg). Deliberately NO single-quote entry — that's the actual fix, not code: the karr #5 rune-literal regression is prevented by omission, not a special case.

func_qr converted from a fixed 'has func_qr' attribute to a per-type method (same style as concat_op/literal_forms): for go it substitutes uppercase L for lowercase l in the alternation ((?:|n|p|np|d|dp|dn|dnp)), N_ family unchanged (already uppercase everywhere). No optional package-alias prefix pattern was needed — verified empirically (against ls.L(...), a bare dot-import L(...), and a foreign x.L(...)) that the leading \b already lands on the '.' separator exactly like it does on PHP's '\\', for the identical reason (not a \w char). Documented alongside the existing php func_qr comment.

New: canonical_func() in Parser.pm, called once in call() right after a func_qr match. Folds go's captured L/Ldnp/... back to lowercase l/ldnp/... (N_ family passed through unchanged) BEFORE required_args() and before storing into found. This means required_args' %arg_lists (Parser.pm) and Scraper.pm's %f (msgid/plural/ctxt/domain position table) needed ZERO go-specific entries — both stay exactly as they were, single source of truth, per the ticket's explicit ask not to triple those tables. Added an explanatory comment above %f in Scraper.pm documenting why it has no go keys.

Scraper.pm: --go=s/$go_ext/push @go,'go'/%e entry mirroring --php exactly; POD extension list + SUPPORTED CALLS section updated, the latter now explicitly notes go's capitalised names as the one accepted name-parity departure (argument shapes/.pot output unaffected).

Fixtures: t/data/n-fixtures/l-calls.go + N-calls.go, both starting with //go:build ignore (verified: 'go build ./t/data/n-fixtures/...' reports 'matched no packages' — the directory is fully invisible to the toolchain, not just excluded-with-warning). 16 forms each (8 canonical shapes × package-qualified 'ls.X(...)' and bare dot-import 'X(...)' styles), one backtick-raw-string literal (domain-only call's msgid), plus the rune-literal regression named in the ticket (for _, c := range "x" { if c == 'a' { ls.L(...) } }) — confirms go's missing single-quote literal_forms entry doesn't let 'a' hijack the string scope before the real call. t/51-scrape-N.t: added go to the language loop, l-calls.go vs N-calls.go produce byte-identical .pot output.

